IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008 (Cth) -- what this Act says to a person who
-- registers as an organ donor: whether the Act sets up or governs the Register they join (it does not mention it); whether it
-- changes the consent needed to remove their organs (s 59(2): it does not); whether keeping their registration is a function
-- the Authority may perform (s 11); whose consent lets the Authority publish information that identifies them (s 58); and,
-- after their death, who their authorised family members are (ss 5, 5A) and who may publish their story (s 58A).
--
-- SEAT: the registering donor -- "Is my registration recorded, and what does it do?". Every decision is phrased as that person
-- would ask it: "Is my registration made under this Act?", "Does this Act change the consent needed to take my organs?",
-- "Whose consent lets the Authority name me?", "Is my brother one of my authorised family members?", "May my family tell my
-- story after I die?". The Act addresses the Authority, its CEO, DonateLife Agencies and grant recipients; what it means for
-- the donor is what may be published about them, and with whose consent. Judgments the Act hands to others (whether a function
-- has been conferred by another law or a Minister's instrument, the constitutional reach of a publication, a person's legal
-- capacity) are asked as facts, never guessed.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4 ("organ or tissue donation and transplantation matter", paras (b), (h)), s 5, s 5A, s 11(1)(d), (l),
-- (m), s 11(2) (as one fact), s 58(1A), (1), (2), (3), s 58A(1), (2), (3), s 59(2).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 9, compilation date 21 February 2024 (register id C2024C00060), includes amendments up to Act
-- No. 58, 2023, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2008A00122.txt. No regulations were retrieved: the persons the
-- regulations may add (s 5(i), s 58(2)(c)) are asked as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Parts 2 (other than s 11) to 6 -- the Authority's establishment, the CEO, staff, the Advisory Board, expert
-- advisory committees and grants -- and ss 1-3, 6, 7, 12, 13, 57, 60: machinery, none of which the donor meets. s 5B-5E
-- (child, parent, sibling, stepchild) are asked as a kind of relationship, not worked out. s 5F (DonateLife Agency) is asked
-- as a fact. s 58(4), s 58A(4)-(6) (the effect on State law; secondary reporting). THE DEPOSITED TEXT DOES NOT MENTION THE
-- AUSTRALIAN ORGAN DONOR REGISTER: the word "Register" appears only for the Federal Register of Legislation. Whether a
-- registration is consent to removal is for State law (s 59(2)); in Western Australia see the Human Tissue and Transplant Act
-- 1982 (WA) baseline encoding, s 22.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008 (Cth)`

§§ `numbers the Act sets`

-- s 58(2)(a): "if the organ or tissue donor or recipient is aged at least 18 years".
`the age of adulthood` MEANS 18

-- s 58(2)(ab): "is under 16 years of age"; (ac), (ad): "is 16 or 17 years of age".
`the age from which capacity counts` MEANS 16

§§ `the donor`

-- One case is one donor (or recipient): the person whose organs or tissue the question is about. "Legal capacity" and "died"
-- are borrowed terms, asked as facts.
DECLARE Donor
    HAS `age` IS A NUMBER
        `has died` IS A BOOLEAN
        `has legal capacity to consent to the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
        `has traditional Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship ties` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is a member of a community that accepts other relationships as kinship ties` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is survived by an authorised family member` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `59(2) -- the Register and consent to removal`

-- s 59(2): "This Act does not affect the operation of: (a) a law of a State or Territory; or (b) a rule of common law; to the
-- extent that the law or rule requires the giving of consent to the removal of an organ or tissue from the body of an
-- individual (whether living or deceased)." s 59(1): the Act "is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of a law of a
-- State or Territory that is capable of operating concurrently".
-- The Act nowhere establishes, names or regulates the Australian Organ Donor Register.
DECLARE `What this Act says my registration does` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: this Act does not mention the Register; whether it counts as consent is for State or Territory law (s 59(2))`

@export Is my organ donor registration made or governed by the Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008?
GIVEN `I am on the Australian Organ Donor Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have registered as a donor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my registration made under this Act` `I am on the Australian Organ Donor Register` IF
    `I am on the Australian Organ Donor Register` AND FALSE

@export What does the Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008 say my donor registration does?
GIVEN `I am on the Australian Organ Donor Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have registered as a donor
GIVETH A `What this Act says my registration does`
DECIDE `What does this Act say my registration does` `I am on the Australian Organ Donor Register` IS
    `nothing: this Act does not mention the Register; whether it counts as consent is for State or Territory law (s 59(2))`

@export Does the Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008 change the consent needed to remove my organs or tissue (s 59(2))?
GIVEN `I am living` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the removal would be while you are alive (otherwise after death)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this Act change the consent needed to remove my organs` `I am living` IF
    -- "whether living or deceased": the answer is the same either way.
    (`I am living` OR (NOT `I am living`)) AND FALSE

§§ `11 -- may the Authority keep my registration?`

-- s 4: "organ or tissue donation and transplantation matter ... includes ... (b) the identification of potential organ or
-- tissue donors; ... (h) public knowledge about, and confidence in, organ or tissue donation and transplantation services."
-- s 11(1): the functions of the Authority are "(d) to collect, analyse, interpret and disseminate information relating to
-- organ or tissue donation and transplantation matters; ... (l) such other functions as are conferred on the Authority by
-- this Act or any other law; and (m) such other functions (if any) as are specified in a written instrument given by the
-- Minister". s 11(2): "The Authority may perform its functions only" with respect to the listed heads of power.
-- READING: a donor registration is "information relating to" the identification of potential donors (para (b)). Whether it is
-- in fact the Authority that keeps the Register is not in the Act: it is asked as a fact.
@export Is keeping my donor registration within the functions this Act gives the Authority (s 11)?
GIVEN `my registration identifies me as a potential donor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what is kept is information about you as a potential donor
      `another law or a Minister's instrument confers the function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another law, or a written instrument of the Minister, gives the Authority the task of keeping the register
      `it is within a head of power in s 11(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether keeping it falls within one of the constitutional heads in s 11(2) (for example the executive power or statistics)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is keeping my registration within the Authority's functions` `my registration identifies me as a potential donor` `another law or a Minister's instrument confers the function` `it is within a head of power in s 11(2)` IF
        (`my registration identifies me as a potential donor` OR `another law or a Minister's instrument confers the function`)
    AND `it is within a head of power in s 11(2)`

§§ `58 -- may the Authority publish information that identifies me?`

-- s 58(1A), (1): the Authority and the CEO "must not publish or disseminate information that is likely to enable the
-- identification of a particular organ or tissue donor or recipient". s 58(2): that does not apply "if the publication or
-- dissemination of the information takes place with the consent of: (a) if the organ or tissue donor or recipient is aged at
-- least 18 years -- the organ or tissue donor or recipient; or (ab) if ... under 16 years of age -- a parent or legal guardian
-- ...; or (ac) if ... (i) is 16 or 17 years of age; and (ii) has legal capacity to consent ...; the organ or tissue donor or
-- recipient; or (ad) if ... 16 or 17 ... and does not have legal capacity ...; a parent or legal guardian ...; or (b) if the
-- organ or tissue donor or recipient has died but is survived by one or more authorised family members -- any of those
-- authorised family members; or (c) in any other case -- an individual who, under the regulations, is authorised".
-- READING: paras (a)-(ad) speak of a living person; (b) and (c) of one who has died.
DECLARE `Whose consent counts` IS ONE OF
    `mine (s 58(2)(a), (ac))`
    `my parent or legal guardian's (s 58(2)(ab), (ad))`
    `any one of my authorised family members' (s 58(2)(b))`
    `an individual the regulations authorise (s 58(2)(c))`

@export Whose consent lets the Authority or its CEO publish information that identifies me as a donor (s 58(2))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Donor @desc Your age, whether you have died, your capacity to consent and whether you leave authorised family members
GIVETH A `Whose consent counts`
DECIDE `Whose consent lets the Authority publish information identifying me` `me` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `me`'s `has died` AND `me`'s `is survived by an authorised family member`
        THEN `any one of my authorised family members' (s 58(2)(b))`
      IF `me`'s `has died`
        THEN `an individual the regulations authorise (s 58(2)(c))`
      IF `me`'s `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood`
        THEN `mine (s 58(2)(a), (ac))`
      IF `me`'s `age` LESS THAN `the age from which capacity counts`
        THEN `my parent or legal guardian's (s 58(2)(ab), (ad))`
      IF `me`'s `has legal capacity to consent to the publication`
        THEN `mine (s 58(2)(a), (ac))`
      OTHERWISE `my parent or legal guardian's (s 58(2)(ab), (ad))`

-- s 58(3): "Subsection (2) does not permit the publication or dissemination by the Authority or the CEO of information that
-- reveals that an organ and/or tissue was: (a) removed from the body of a particular organ or tissue donor; and (b)
-- transplanted to the body of a particular organ or tissue recipient." No consent unlocks the donor-recipient match.
@export May the Authority or its CEO publish information that identifies me as a donor (s 58)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Donor @desc Your age, whether you have died, your capacity to consent and whether you leave authorised family members
      `the person whose consent counts has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person s 58(2) names (you, a parent or guardian, a family member) has consented
      `it reveals which recipient received my organ or tissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it would reveal that an organ or tissue went from you to a particular recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Authority publish information identifying me` `me` `the person whose consent counts has consented` `it reveals which recipient received my organ or tissue` IF
        `the person whose consent counts has consented`
    AND (NOT `it reveals which recipient received my organ or tissue`)

§§ `5, 5A -- my authorised family members, after my death`

-- s 5: "authorised family member of an organ or tissue donor or recipient who has died means any of the following persons:
-- (a) the partner ...; (b) a parent or legal guardian ...; (c) a child ...; (d) a sibling ...; (e) a grandparent ...; (f) a
-- grandchild ...; (g) if the organ or tissue donor or recipient has traditional Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship
-- ties -- a person who is related ... under Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules; (h) if the organ or tissue
-- donor or recipient is a member of a community that accepts relationships other than those referred to in paragraphs (a) to
-- (g) as kinship ties -- a person who is accepted by the community to be related ...; (i) a person who, under the regulations,
-- is taken to be an authorised family member". No paragraph sets a minimum age.
-- s 5A(1): "partner of a person means: (a) the person's spouse; or (b) the person's de facto partner." s 5A(2): "if more than
-- one person would qualify as a partner ... only the last person to so qualify is the partner".
-- ss 5B-5E widen "child", "parent", "sibling" and "stepchild" (adopted, step, foster, half and so on); the relationship is
-- asked as a fact already so widened.
DECLARE Relationship IS ONE OF
    `spouse or de facto partner`
    `former spouse or former de facto partner`
    `parent or legal guardian`
    `child`
    `sibling`
    `grandparent`
    `grandchild`
    `related under Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules`
    `accepted by my community as related`
    `taken by the regulations to be an authorised family member`
    `friend or other person`

DECLARE Relative
    HAS `relationship` IS A Relationship
        `age` IS A NUMBER
        `is the last person to qualify as my partner` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is this person one of my authorised family members under the Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority Act 2008 (s 5)?
GIVEN `them` IS A Relative @desc Who they are to you
      `me` IS A Donor @desc Whether you have died, and your kinship ties
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person one of my authorised family members` `them` `me` IF
        `me`'s `has died`
    AND (CONSIDER `them`'s `relationship`
         WHEN `spouse or de facto partner` THEN `them`'s `is the last person to qualify as my partner`
         WHEN `parent or legal guardian` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `sibling` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `grandparent` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `grandchild` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `related under Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules` THEN `me`'s `has traditional Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship ties`
         WHEN `accepted by my community as related` THEN `me`'s `is a member of a community that accepts other relationships as kinship ties`
         WHEN `taken by the regulations to be an authorised family member` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `58A -- who may tell my story after my death`

-- s 58A(1): "This section applies if: (a) an organ or tissue donation and transplantation has occurred; and (b) the organ or
-- tissue donor or recipient has died." Each permission is for one of four purposes: "(i) an educational activity ...; (ii) a
-- commemorative activity ...; (iii) a promotional activity ...; (iv) a community awareness activity" relevant to (or, for
-- commemoration, that is) an organ or tissue donation and transplantation matter.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `an educational activity`
    `a commemorative activity`
    `a promotional activity`
    `a community awareness activity`
    `some other purpose`

GIVEN p IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the four activities` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `some other purpose` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `me` IS A Donor
      `a donation and transplantation has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 58A applies to me` `me` `a donation and transplantation has occurred` IF
    `a donation and transplantation has occurred` AND `me`'s `has died`

-- s 58A(3): "An authorised family member ... may publish, disseminate or disclose information that is likely to enable the
-- identification of the deceased ... if: (a) the publication ... is for the purposes of any of the following activities of
-- the Authority or a DonateLife Agency: [the four]; and (b) the publication ... is made: (i) using a service to which paragraph
-- 51(v) of the Constitution applies; or (ii) using an electronic service (within the meaning of the Online Safety Act 2021);
-- or (iii) in a Territory; or (iv) in a Commonwealth place". Para (b) is asked as one fact.
@export After my death as a donor, may this member of my family publish information that identifies me (s 58A(3))?
GIVEN `them` IS A Relative @desc Who they are to you
      `me` IS A Donor @desc Whether you have died, and your kinship ties
      `a donation and transplantation has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your organs or tissue were in fact removed and transplanted
      `the purpose` IS A Purpose @desc What the publication is for
      `it is an activity of the Authority or a DonateLife Agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activity is one run by the Authority or a DonateLife Agency
      `it is made by a means s 58A(3)(b) names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is published by phone, post, broadcast or an electronic service, or in a Territory or Commonwealth place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my family member publish information identifying me` `them` `me` `a donation and transplantation has occurred` `the purpose` `it is an activity of the Authority or a DonateLife Agency` `it is made by a means s 58A(3)(b) names` IF
        `section 58A applies to me` `me` `a donation and transplantation has occurred`
    AND `Is this person one of my authorised family members` `them` `me`
    AND `is one of the four activities` `the purpose`
    AND `it is an activity of the Authority or a DonateLife Agency`
    AND `it is made by a means s 58A(3)(b) names`

-- s 58A(2): "a DonateLife Agency" or a person party to an agreement in force providing for grants under s 11(1)(g) "may
-- publish ... if: (c) [for one of the four purposes]; and (d) the publication ... is made with the consent of an authorised
-- family member of the deceased ...; and (e) the publication ... is made: [the s 58A(3)(b) means, or] (v) by a constitutional
-- corporation". Para (e) is asked as one fact.
@export After my death as a donor, may a DonateLife Agency or a grant recipient publish information that identifies me (s 58A(2))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Donor @desc Whether you have died
      `a donation and transplantation has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your organs or tissue were in fact removed and transplanted
      `the publisher is a DonateLife Agency or a grant recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher is a declared DonateLife Agency, or a party to a grant agreement in force under s 11(1)(g)
      `the purpose` IS A Purpose @desc What the publication is for
      `an authorised family member of mine consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of your authorised family members consents
      `it is made by a means s 58A(2)(e) names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is published by phone, post, broadcast or an electronic service, in a Territory or Commonwealth place, or by a constitutional corporation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a DonateLife Agency publish information identifying me` `me` `a donation and transplantation has occurred` `the publisher is a DonateLife Agency or a grant recipient` `the purpose` `an authorised family member of mine consents` `it is made by a means s 58A(2)(e) names` IF
        `section 58A applies to me` `me` `a donation and transplantation has occurred`
    AND `the publisher is a DonateLife Agency or a grant recipient`
    AND `is one of the four activities` `the purpose`
    AND `an authorised family member of mine consents`
    AND `it is made by a means s 58A(2)(e) names`
